 the anchor points at the emitter, not `write_jira_config`.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.0928,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"`_config_writer._emit_toml` (:188) fail-closes on any nested sub-table\" and \"_emit_toml (:188) ... stay UNTOUCHED\"","src/rebar/_config_writer.py:32 defines `def _emit_toml(data: dict) -> str:`","src/rebar/_config_writer.py:180 defines `def write_jira_config(`"],"finding":"The plan cites `_config_writer._emit_toml` at line :188, but `_emit_toml` is defined at `_config_writer.py:32`; line :180/:188 is the `write_jira_config` region.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2de50ce85f7587d7","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — Serialization; Scope bullet 2","norm_id":"ncb96f5e0b8d95b3f","priority":0.6072,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer/implementer jumps to _config_writer.py:188 expecting _emit_toml and lands inside write_jira_config"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Change `_emit_toml (:188)` references to `_emit_toml (:32)`.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7143,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Attribute the `_passthrough`/`_passthrough_help` dispatch branch to `_cli/_bridge_commands.py` (where `bridge_cli` and both helpers live) and keep only the `_bridge_suggest_mapping` handler in `_cli/__init__.py`.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"add ... a `_passthrough`/`_passthrough_help` branch → NEW handler `_bridge_suggest_mapping` (`_cli/__init__.py`, sibling of `_bridge_probe`)\"","search of _cli/__init__.py for `_passthrough` returns (no matches)","_bridge_commands.py:95 `def _passthrough`, :114 `def _passthrough_help`, :263-266 the `{fsck, check-access, setup, suggest-mapping}` branch calling them"],"finding":"The plan locates the `_passthrough`/`_passthrough_help` dispatch branch in `_cli/__init__.py`, but that branch and both helpers live in `_cli/_bridge_commands.py` (`bridge_cli`); only the `_bridge_suggest_mapping` handler belongs in `__init__.py`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8b1f18142ebccbea","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — Dispatch bullet","norm_id":"nbe492b8577f020b2","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer edits __init__.py to add the pass-through branch and can't find _passthrough there"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Reword to: add the branch in `_bridge_commands.py`'s `bridge_cli` (beside the existing fsck/check-access/setup pass-through at :263) calling `_passthrough`/`_passthrough_help`; the NEW `_bridge_suggest_mapping` handler goes in `_cli/__init__.py`.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4286,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the deep-merge rule for list-valued vocabulary keys (statuses/issue_types/link_types) when the target already has them — e.g. existing list wins wholesale, or union with a documented ordering — and pin it with a test case.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.4763,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'DEEP-MERGE under data[\"mapping\"][\"projects\"][<KEY>] (EXISTING keys win, hand edits never clobbered)'","Vocabulary layers (statuses, issue_types, link_types) are lists; 'existing keys win' is unambiguous for scalar/dict keys but a list under an existing key could mean skip-entirely, replace, or union — each yields a materially different re-probe result","AC test_probe_write_preserves_edits exercises a pre-existing hand-edited mapping KEY but does not pin list-merge behavior"],"finding":"The --write deep-merge specifies 'existing keys win' for scalar/table keys but does not define merge semantics for list-valued vocabulary keys (statuses, issue_types, link_types) when the target already contains them from a prior probe or hand edit.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f42c96a63b4f20f2a","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Emit section: 'DEEP-MERGE under data[\"mapping\"][\"projects\"][<KEY>] (EXISTING keys win)'","norm_id":"n642db3fa0260d3b6","priority":0.1237,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator re-runs suggest-mapping --write after adding a new issue type in Jira; the existing statuses/issue_types list either silently stays stale (skip) or drops hand-added entries (replace)"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Address the deprecation/removal of `createmeta_issuetypes`/`createmeta_fieldtypes`: justify their use vs the successor `project_issue_types()`/`project_issue_fields()` and account for Jira 9.0+ DC removal of the createmeta REST endpoint (the plan's target platform).","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'create_defaults stubs → jira.JIRA.createmeta_issuetypes(<KEY>) + createmeta_fieldtypes(<KEY>, <id>) (public createmeta API)'","pycontribs/jira discussion #1796 and issue #1802: 'v3.6.0 removed the createmeta methods (createmeta_issuetypes and createmeta_fieldtypes) and replaced them with two new methods (project_issue_types and project_issue_fields)'","jira.readthedocs client source: \"createmeta_fieldtypes' is deprecated and will be removed in future releases. Use 'project_issue_fields' instead\" (DeprecationWarning)","Inflectra KB687: createmeta endpoint 'has been removed from Jira 9.0 or later ... This also affects Jira Data Center'; pycontribs issue #840: deprecated, admin-disablable since 8.4.0","Repo: adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py:155 build_client_from_settings targets Jira DC (Bearer PAT, Jira 8.14+) — the platform where createmeta is removed"],"finding":"The `create_defaults` axis is grounded on `jira.JIRA.createmeta_issuetypes` / `createmeta_fieldtypes`, described as 'public createmeta API', but these pycontribs methods are deprecated as of jira 3.6.0 (inside the pinned >=3.8,<4 range) with successors `project_issue_types()`/`project_issue_fields()`, and the underlying `/rest/api/2/issue/createmeta` REST endpoint was removed in Jira 9.0+ for Server AND Data Center — which is the plan's own target platform.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f61c541f362fa32b4","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Axis grounding, `create_defaults` bullet; Scope pin `jira>=3.8,<4`","norm_id":"n5a18c08471dbe8f0","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Running `rebar bridge suggest-mapping <KEY>` against a real Jira DC 9.0+ instance where the createmeta endpoint has been removed or admin-disabled","Upgrading the pinned jira dependency toward a future release that removes the deprecated createmeta_* methods"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Ground the create_defaults axis on the non-deprecated `jira.JIRA.project_issue_types()` / `project_issue_fields()` (with a documented fallback + graceful-drop note when the endpoint is unavailable), rather than the deprecated createmeta_* methods; verify the chosen methods exist across the pinned >=3.8,<4 range.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.45,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Anchor each asserted pycontribs `jira.JIRA` method (`issue_types`, `priorities`, `issue_link_types`, `statuses`, `createmeta_issuetypes`, `createmeta_fieldtypes`) to a version-pinned doc reference or an existing in-repo call site, and classify each as MATCH/UNVERIFIED against pycontribs 3.8–<4 for Jira Data Center specifically.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the vocabulary getters are documented pycontribs 3.x public API' — no version-pinned doc anchor supplied.","In-repo VERIFIED: search_issues (adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py:279), transitions (adapters/jira_datacenter/transitions.py:80).","UNVERIFIED (endpoint-granularity axis, new surface on used vendor): issue_types(), priorities(), issue_link_types(), statuses(), createmeta_issuetypes(), createmeta_fieldtypes() — not used elsewhere in adapter; `jira` not importable here (resolve_symbol UNRESOLVED), so existence cannot be confirmed and is NOT asserted a mismatch.","createmeta method naming/shape differs Cloud vs DC and across pycontribs releases within the pinned 3.8–3.x range."],"finding":"The plan asserts several pycontribs `jira.JIRA` vocabulary/createmeta methods exist as 'documented pycontribs 3.x public API' but anchors none of them (no doc citation or in-repo use), and they are not exercised anywhere else in the adapter; only `search_issues` and `transitions` are confirmed in-repo. The `createmeta_issuetypes`/`createmeta_fieldtypes` surface in particular varies by pycontribs version and by Jira Cloud vs Data Center (this adapter targets DC).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe3fc8ee4c0d99909","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Axis grounding' bullets; 'create_defaults' stubs bullet","norm_id":"nab9aef3f8721a609","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A vocab getter name is wrong on the pinned pycontribs release → AttributeError at first live run against a real project.","createmeta_fieldtypes behaves differently (removed/renamed/paginating) on Jira DC vs Cloud → required-field detection silently returns nothing and no create_defaults stubs are emitted."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a doc-anchored verification note per getter (pycontribs 3.x method table) and, for the createmeta pair (the highest-variance surface across Cloud/DC and pycontribs versions), route a small SPIKE to confirm the exact method names/return shape on a real DC instance before committing the stub-emission logic.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.55,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_ex